/target
/.worktrees
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.env
secrets.env
*.vault
.tengu-attachments
/hypothesis
lastrun.md
.tengu/worktrees/
.tengu/scratch/
.tengu/registry-fingerprint
# Editor/vault noise + `tengu skill evolve` scratch output — never repo state.
**/.obsidian/
*.tmp
.tengu/evolve-out/

# Eval runner artifacts (per-run transcripts + report.json). The eval
# runner auto-prunes to `--keep-runs` (default 10), but gitignore keeps
# them out of status/commits regardless.
/evals/runs/

# Skill lifecycle per-run artifacts. The rolling metrics.json + history.jsonl
# are intentional persistent state and remain tracked; only the per-run
# detail dirs are transient.
/skills/*/metrics/runs/

# Claude Code per-user settings (settings.local.json holds approved tool
# allow-lists for the local workstation; not portable across machines).
/.claude/

# Codex CLI per-user settings (mirror of the /.claude/ rule above).
/.codex/

# Agentic memory — planner-context files regenerated on every planner turn
# (TENGU_PLANNER_REGISTRY.md from agents/skills/tools, TENGU_PLAN.md from the
# current accepted plan). Pure runtime artifacts; never hand-edited.
/TENGU_PLANNER_REGISTRY.md
/TENGU_PLAN.md

# Agentic memory — raw ingested sources. May contain arbitrary payloads
# (files, URLs, transcripts) including sensitive content — same reasoning as
# the cache.db rule below. The compiled wiki under .tengu/agentic-memory/wiki/
# is intentionally NOT ignored: it is human-reviewable via git diff (PRD).
**/.tengu/agentic-memory/raw/

# Runtime caches written by the `shared_cache` / `persistent_store` plugins.
# These live under `<agent.workspace>/.tengu/cache.db` and can contain
# arbitrary tool-output snippets, including sensitive payloads from
# webhook bodies, http_request responses, etc. The repo's normal `.tengu/`
# entries above cover registry-fingerprint / scratch / worktrees at the
# repo root; this pattern catches `.tengu/cache.db` no matter where in
# the worktree it ends up (e.g. under a bogus `~` directory if some code
# path forgot `expand_tilde` — see 2026-05-11 fix in webhook_builder.rs).
**/.tengu/cache.db
# Defensive catch-all for the broken-tilde case ONLY (real workspaces
# under `~/aura-workspace/...` etc. live OUTSIDE the repo and aren't
# git-visible — we only need to ignore the literal `~` directory that
# pre-fix runs created at the repo root).
/~/
